    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM7wWCw4",
      "title": "Bump superchain-registry submodule to fix check_superchain_registry drift",
      "author": "claude",
      "number": 1496,
      "body": "<!-- ccr-slack-attribution -->\n_Requested via [Slack thread](https://oplabs-pbc.slack.com/archives/C03N11M0BBN/p1783715169668939?thread_ts=1783715169.668939&cid=C03N11M0BBN)_\n\n## Summary\n\nBumps the pinned `lib/superchain-registry` submodule to current upstream `main` to fix the failing `check_superchain_registry` CI job. This is registry drift, not a superchain-ops code change.\n\n**Before:** The `check_superchain_registry` CI job fails because the pinned registry (`3d29f56`) lists rehearsal chains `420120009`/`420120010` (rehearsal-0-bn-0/1) that upstream `superchain-registry@main` removed. `src/script/check-superchain-latest.sh` hard-fails when a chain present in the pinned `addresses.json` is absent upstream (\"remote missing ...\"), so it exits 1.\n\n**After:** The submodule is bumped to current upstream `main` (`cf72a43`, \"superchain: remove rehearsal-0-bn networks\"), so the pinned chain set matches upstream and the check passes.\n\n**How:** Bumped the `lib/superchain-registry` gitlink from `3d29f56` to `cf72a43`. No script changes. Verified only the gitlink changed and that chains `420120009`/`420120010` are absent from upstream's `addresses.json` at the new commit. Also confirmed no in-repo task references the removed chain IDs.\n\nThis PR also adds a Claude Code skill at `.claude/skills/fix-check-superchain-registry/SKILL.md` documenting how to diagnose and fix this failure (the CI chain, a local reproduction, and the one-line submodule-bump fix) so future agents can resolve recurrences quickly.\n\n---\n\n## Additional context\n\nThe `check_superchain_registry` check is structurally strict: it tolerates upstream having *extra* chains, but hard-fails whenever the pinned file lists a chain that upstream has *removed*. This asymmetry is the recurring cause of this failure. A possible follow-up for maintainers (intentionally **not** implemented here) is to treat upstream chain removals as a warning rather than a hard failure, while still hard-failing on address mismatches.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01GmpmyVwe1ykHbjjnrTf2C9\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01GmpmyVwe1ykHbjjnrTf2C9)_",
